<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <title>Mary Borji - Evidence Checklist and Next Steps</title>
  <style>
    body{font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;color:#111827;line-height:1.48;margin:42px;font-size:13.5px}
    h1{color:#0052a4;font-size:24px}h2{color:#0052a4;font-size:18px;margin-top:24px}
    table{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;margin:10px 0 16px}th{background:#0052a4;color:#fff;text-align:left;padding:8px;border:1px solid #cbd5e1}td{padding:8px;border:1px solid #cbd5e1;vertical-align:top}
    .box{background:#eef6ff;border-left:4px solid #0052a4;padding:10px 12px;margin:12px 0}
    li{margin:5px 0}
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <h1>Evidence Checklist and Next Steps</h1>
  <p><strong>Client:</strong> Mrs Mary Borji<br>
  <strong>Property:</strong> 11 Richland Road, Liverpool, L13 7BN<br>
  <strong>Issue:</strong> Spray foam loft insulation, humidity, timber deterioration and roof replacement loss.</p>

  <h2>1. Priority Documents to Obtain</h2>
  <table>
    <tr><th>Document</th><th>Why it matters</th><th>Status</th></tr>
    <tr><td>Protect Insulation Services Ltd quote, contract and invoice</td><td>Shows who sold/installed the product, price and terms.</td><td>TBC</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Green Homes Scheme grant voucher</td><td>Shows funding route, scheme obligations and possible approved-installer information.</td><td>Client says available</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Proof of payment / grant payment record</td><td>Shows payment of GBP 7,350 and source of funds.</td><td>TBC</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Warranty or guarantee paperwork</td><td>May identify warranty provider, complaints route or insurance-backed guarantee.</td><td>TBC</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Pre-installation survey or suitability assessment</td><td>Key evidence on whether roof condition and ventilation were checked before installation.</td><td>TBC</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Roofing report / inspection letter</td><td>Should confirm humidity, timber deterioration and whether spray foam contributed to the issue.</td><td>TBC</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Roof replacement invoice and payment proof</td><td>Supports GBP 5,800 roof replacement loss.</td><td>TBC</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Photographs</td><td>Shows spray foam remaining on loft floor, joists, dividing wall, timbers and visible damage.</td><td>Client says available</td></tr>
  </table>

  <h2>2. Key Questions for Mrs Borji</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Who attended the property and sold the spray foam?</li>
    <li>Was any roof survey carried out before installation?</li>
    <li>Was Mrs Borji warned about moisture, timber deterioration, mortgage issues, sale issues or future roof repair problems?</li>
    <li>Was the Green Homes Scheme voucher issued directly to Mrs Borji or to the installer?</li>
    <li>Does the voucher name Protect Insulation Services Ltd or another company?</li>
    <li>Who carried out the January 2026 roof replacement?</li>
    <li>Can the roofer provide a short written report linking the damage to humidity, ventilation and/or spray foam?</li>
    <li>Is spray foam still present and can additional photographs be taken before any further removal?</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>3. Suggested Complaint Attachments</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Copy of the formal complaint letter.</li>
    <li>Green Homes Scheme grant voucher.</li>
    <li>Installation quote, contract and invoice.</li>
    <li>Roof replacement quote/invoice for GBP 5,800.</li>
    <li>Photographs of the damage and remaining spray foam.</li>
    <li>Any roofing inspection or survey comments.</li>
    <li>Any warranty, guarantee or sales literature.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>4. Practical Next Steps</h2>
  <div class="box">
    <ol>
      <li>Confirm the full legal name, address and company number of Protect Insulation Services Ltd.</li>
      <li>Send the formal complaint letter with the key evidence available now.</li>
      <li>Ask the roofing contractor for a short written causation statement.</li>
      <li>Check whether the Green Homes Scheme or grant administrator has a complaint process or installer standards route.</li>
      <li>Check for warranty/insurance-backed guarantee routes.</li>
      <li>Update the loss schedule if further removal, remediation, inspection or repair costs arise.</li>
    </ol>
  </div>

  <h2>5. Current Loss Schedule</h2>
  <table>
    <tr><th>Loss item</th><th>Amount</th><th>Evidence required</th></tr>
    <tr><td>Spray foam installation / Green Homes Scheme works</td><td>GBP 7,350</td><td>Grant voucher, invoice, payment proof.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Roof replacement / remedial works</td><td>GBP 5,800</td><td>Invoice, quote, payment proof and roofer report.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Total currently identified</td><td>GBP 13,150</td><td>Subject to evidence and recoverability.</td></tr>
  </table>
</body>
</html>
